",".py","maintainability","nested-control-flow","basic-cocomo-organic","7.29.15","js-security","actions-security","npm-supply-chain","dockerfile","1.1.0","1.27.0","3.11.8","check","aws-access-key-id","secret","Flags AWS access key IDs (AKIA or ASIA followed by 16 base32 characters); lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","aws-secret-access-key","Flags a 40-character base64 value assigned to an AWS secret access key name; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","github-token","Flags GitHub personal access, OAuth, user, server and refresh tokens (ghp_, gho_, ghu_, ghs_, ghr_, github_pat_); lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","gitlab-token","Flags GitLab personal access tokens (glpat- followed by at least 20 characters); lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","slack-token","Flags Slack bot, user, app, refresh and legacy tokens (xoxb-, xoxp-, xoxa-, xoxr-, xoxs-); lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","slack-webhook","Flags Slack incoming webhook, workflow and trigger URLs on hooks.slack.com; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","stripe-secret-key","Flags Stripe live secret and restricted keys (sk_live_, rk_live_); test and publishable keys are ignored; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","google-api-key","Flags Google API keys (AIza followed by 35 characters), often meant for clients but still worth restricting; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","npm-token","Flags npm access tokens (npm_ followed by 36 characters); lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","private-key","Flags PEM, OpenSSH and PGP private key blocks that have a base64 body and a footer; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","jwt","Flags JSON Web Tokens whose first segment decodes to a JSON header with an alg field; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","generic-secret-assignment","Flags a quoted high-entropy literal of 16 or more characters assigned to a password, secret, token or API key name, ignoring placeholders such as example, dummy, changeme, xxx, ${...} and process.env; lines containing repometry-ignore-secret are skipped.","sensitive-file","Flags files that usually hold credentials: .env and .env.* except .env.example, .env.sample and .env.template, *.pem and *.key unless they hold only public certificates or keys, *.p12, *.pfx, id_rsa, id_dsa, id_ecdsa, id_ed25519, .git-credentials, and .npmrc or .pypirc with a literal auth token; repometry-ignore-secret on the first line skips the file.","eval","security","eval() or the Function constructor runs a string that is not a literal, so injected text becomes code.","child-process-injection","child_process exec or execSync runs a shell command built from interpolated or concatenated values.","vm-code-execution","The vm module compiles or runs code that is not a literal, and vm is not a security boundary.","dom-xss","Markup that is not a literal is written through innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML or document.write.","tls-verification-disabled","TLS certificate verification is turned off with rejectUnauthorized or NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED.","weak-hash","createHash or createHmac uses the broken MD5 or SHA-1 algorithm.","insecure-random","Math.random() feeds a value named like a token, secret, password, nonce, salt, key or one-time code.","http-url","A string literal points at a plain http:// URL on a public host.","unpinned-action","infrastructure","A third-party action or reusable workflow is referenced by a tag or branch instead of a full commit SHA.","unpinned-first-party-action","An action owned by actions or github is referenced by a tag or branch instead of a full commit SHA.","script-injection","A run script expands attacker-controlled context, such as an issue title or a branch name, directly into the shell.","pull-request-target-checkout","A pull_request_target or workflow_run workflow checks out untrusted pull request code in a privileged job.","excessive-permissions","The workflow or one of its jobs grants the GITHUB_TOKEN write-all permissions.","missing-permissions","Neither the workflow nor any of its jobs declares permissions, so the GITHUB_TOKEN gets the repository default.","persisted-credentials","An actions/checkout step leaves the GITHUB_TOKEN in the git config because persist-credentials is not false.","secrets-inherit","A reusable workflow call passes every repository secret with secrets: inherit.","dependency-from-url","dependency","A package.json dependency is installed from a URL, git repository or tarball instead of a registry version.","dependency-unbounded","A package.json dependency accepts any version through \"*\", \"latest\" or an empty range.","install-script","A package.json declares a preinstall, install or postinstall script that runs whenever the package is installed.","lockfile-insecure-registry","A lockfile resolves a package over unencrypted HTTP or git transport.","lockfile-foreign-host","A lockfile resolves a package from a host other than the public npm or Yarn registry.","lockfile-missing-integrity","A package-lock entry resolved from a registry has no integrity hash.","unpinned-base-image","A FROM image has no tag or uses latest and is not pinned by digest, so rebuilds can silently change the base.","runs-as-root","The final stage sets no USER or switches back to root, so the container runs as root.","remote-add","ADD downloads a remote URL without checksum verification instead of curl with a checksum or COPY.","pipe-to-shell","A RUN step pipes a curl or wget download straight into a shell, executing unverified remote code.","secret-in-env","An ENV or ARG with a secret-looking name carries a literal value that is stored in the image or its history.","apt-unpinned-upgrade","A RUN step runs apt-get upgrade or dist-upgrade, so the image contents depend on the day it was built.","sudo-usage","A RUN step uses sudo, which is unnecessary du